<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 40,631 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 40,631 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 40,631 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday, compared to 59,836 tonnes on in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Sunday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			16,894	    7,938</p>
<p>    Import cargo			23,737	   80,165</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, seven ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, four ships were expected to sail and eight were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>High speed deisel    73,000	 Chesapeak City     due</p>
<p>Crude oil		71,000	 Stavros-1	    due</p>
<p>Jet feul		 25,000	 Ras Al-Zour	  3/2</p>
<p>Palm oil		 15,000	 Wawasan Megah     29/1</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Keefan		 7/2</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasan Courage    5/2</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
